cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use CountryCode-Decide, please cite it as below.
title: 'CountryCode-Decide: messy country names to ISO 3166 codes, with calibrated abstention'
authors:
- family-names: Ildan
  given-names: Ali
version: 1.2.1
date-released: '2026-10-10'
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: https://github.com/aliildan/country-code-decide
url: https://huggingface.co/aildan/country-code-decide-small
abstract: A small open-weight model (mmBERT-small, 8-bit ONNX, CPU) that maps a country or US state written
  as free text in company registers and forms (any language or script, misspelled, abbreviated, historical)
  to ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 and ISO 3166-2:US codes with calibrated probabilities, and abstains with a short
  candidate list when a certified error-rate target cannot be met. Training combines Unicode CLDR and
  Wikidata names, real register strings and generated variants that passed quality gates and a human label
  audit; answer thresholds are certified by fixed-sequence testing on held-out real register strings;
  evaluation uses fresh registers read once after a frozen pre-registration.
keywords:
- ISO 3166
- country codes
- entity normalization
- know-your-business
- company registers
- calibration
- selective prediction
- abstention
- Learn-then-Test
